Package: fev1pexa
Title: Individualized FEV1 Decline Prediction in COPD - ModelsCloud Wrapper
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Ramin", "Rezaeianzadeh", email = "raminrzn@student.ubc.ca",
           role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Zafar", "Zafari", role = "ctb",
           comment = "Author of the underlying FEV1 decline model"),
    person("Amin", "Adibi", role = "ctb",
           comment = "Author of the fev1 package this wrapper calls"),
    person("Mohsen", "Sadatsafavi", role = "ctb"))
Description: A ModelsCloud wrapper for the 'fev1' package, which implements
    the individualized prediction of lung-function decline in chronic
    obstructive pulmonary disease described in Zafari et al. (CMAJ 2016)
    <doi:10.1503/cmaj.151483>. Projects a patient's FEV1 trajectory over a
    16-year horizon under two scenarios, continued smoking and sustained
    quitting, with 95% prediction intervals. The model itself lives in
    resplab/fev1; this package only adapts it to the ModelsCloud calling
    convention (model_run(), get_sample_input(), get_default_input()) and
    adds the gateway entry point the platform dispatches to.
